WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:08.530
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:08.800 --> 03:12.040
So you're going home? Your husband isn't trying to stop you?

3
03:12.120 --> 03:13.320
I'll serve it for you, Grandpa.

4
03:13.400 --> 03:14.640
No need.

5
03:14.720 --> 03:17.040
I already drink a tonic every day.

6
03:17.120 --> 03:22.320
Before Hathaya left, she bought the herbs and asked the maid

7
03:22.400 --> 03:24.120
to prepare them for me every day.

8
03:24.200 --> 03:25.160
Be patient, sweetheart.

9
03:26.480 --> 03:29.160
PREVIOUSLY

10
03:29.240 --> 03:30.600
Grandma!

11
03:43.000 --> 03:44.800
May the sacred spirits

12
03:44.880 --> 03:48.600
and guardian deities of this place

13
03:49.800 --> 03:54.160
protect my grandmother and keep her safe.

14
03:55.080 --> 03:56.520
Please let her…

15
03:58.040 --> 04:00.960
recover quickly. Please guide the doctors…

16
04:02.280 --> 04:06.360
so they can heal her and make her strong again.

17
04:10.800 --> 04:13.080
May all the good deeds I have done

18
04:13.160 --> 04:16.839
in past lives and in this life

19
04:18.240 --> 04:22.000
bring merit to my grandmother.

20
04:23.200 --> 04:26.600
Please let her live and regain her strength.

21
04:52.280 --> 04:56.360
Grandma Duangjai is a good person who has always thought and done good.

22
05:01.840 --> 05:04.320
May the guardian spirits protect

23
05:04.920 --> 05:06.840
the life of such a good person.

24
05:07.440 --> 05:09.360
Sadhu.

25
05:29.520 --> 05:30.560
Here.

26
05:31.600 --> 05:32.560
Food.

27
05:33.080 --> 05:35.480
I can't eat. You take it.

28
05:36.160 --> 05:38.400
Take it.

29
05:38.480 --> 05:39.560
Here's some water too.

30
05:45.120 --> 05:47.400
When your grandma gets better,

31
05:48.280 --> 05:52.040
she'll need someone to take care of her. If you get sick,

32
05:52.680 --> 05:54.080
who's going to look after her?

33
05:55.520 --> 05:56.640
Eat.

34
06:08.000 --> 06:09.040
Come on.

35
06:09.840 --> 06:12.640
I know you want to stay close to your grandma,

36
06:13.280 --> 06:14.640
but no need to eat so fast.

37
06:14.720 --> 06:19.840
Slow down, or you'll choke. We barely have doctors here. Slow down.

38
06:22.920 --> 06:24.040
Earlier,

39
06:25.680 --> 06:27.200
when you were praying,

40
06:27.960 --> 06:32.400
you said my grandma is a good person who thinks and does good.

41
06:34.000 --> 06:35.840
How do you know what she's like?

42
06:38.120 --> 06:39.200
I've met her before.

43
06:41.680 --> 06:43.280
You know my grandma?

44
06:46.240 --> 06:48.760
How come I never knew about this?

45
06:50.160 --> 06:53.440
I want to know who Hathaya's mother is living with

46
06:53.520 --> 06:55.680
and whether her grandmother is really sick.

47
07:01.360 --> 07:02.360
Here, Grandma.

48
07:03.640 --> 07:04.920
Use this as capital for your stall

49
07:05.560 --> 07:06.880
so you won't have to borrow from anyone.

50
07:08.120 --> 07:10.560
Well, it was a secret.

51
07:11.480 --> 07:14.680
Mr. Pichai ordered me to investigate your situation.

52
07:14.760 --> 07:18.880
That's how he learned you weren't lying and that everything you said was true.

53
07:24.720 --> 07:25.800
Thank you.

54
07:27.840 --> 07:28.960
You're…

55
07:31.080 --> 07:32.480
not angry

56
07:32.560 --> 07:36.960
that I was investigating you?

57
07:41.320 --> 07:44.600
At least now I know Grandpa doesn't hate me.

58
07:45.640 --> 07:50.040
And Grandpa knows everything I told him was true.

59
07:50.680 --> 07:53.000
Listen to me.

60
07:53.720 --> 07:56.480
Mr. Pichai cares about you.

61
07:56.560 --> 07:59.840
Otherwise, he never would've sent me to investigate your situation.

62
08:07.480 --> 08:08.720
We have to share the water. There's only one bottle.

63
08:31.440 --> 08:34.080
Doctor, the patient's pulse is dropping.

64
08:40.080 --> 08:42.799
Is the doctor here yet? Patient in critical condition.

65
08:42.880 --> 08:44.120
RECORDING IS PROHIBITED

66
08:44.200 --> 08:46.160
Have the doctor come immediately once finished.

67
08:47.040 --> 08:49.480
Nurse, is the doctor here yet?

68
08:49.560 --> 08:53.640
The doctor is in surgery right now. The doctor will come as soon as possible.

69
08:56.160 --> 08:58.480
We have to transfer your grandma to a private hospital.

70
08:58.560 --> 09:00.880
No. I can't let you do that for me.

71
09:05.960 --> 09:09.360
She has to be transferred. That's an order.

72
09:11.640 --> 09:12.520
Grandpa.

73
09:13.160 --> 09:18.200
Transfer her now. Take her to a private hospital with proper equipment.

74
09:19.200 --> 09:20.840
I'll cover all the expenses.

75
09:23.320 --> 09:24.600
Yes, Grandpa.

76
09:25.360 --> 09:27.600
Nurse.

77
10:01.600 --> 10:03.560
Doctor, how is my grandmother?

78
10:04.200 --> 10:06.600
She was brought in just in time.

79
10:06.680 --> 10:08.120
She's safe now.

80
10:08.200 --> 10:12.320
After she rests and recovers here for a bit, she should be able to go home.

81
10:13.040 --> 10:14.640
Thank you so much, Doctor.

82
10:14.720 --> 10:15.720
You're welcome.

83
10:31.440 --> 10:32.720
Grandpa,

84
10:33.600 --> 10:35.360
Grandma is safe now.

85
10:42.840 --> 10:47.040
Grandpa, thank you so much for saving Grandma.

86
10:47.120 --> 10:50.640
If you hadn't helped her, I don't know what would have happened to her.

87
10:50.720 --> 10:52.680
Thank you so much, Grandpa.

88
10:52.760 --> 10:54.600
All right.

89
10:54.680 --> 10:56.760
Get up, Hathaya.

90
10:59.640 --> 11:02.360
Hathaya. I said get up.

91
11:06.000 --> 11:07.680
You don't have to thank me.

92
11:08.520 --> 11:12.960
After all, Duangjai was once my son's mother-in-law.

93
11:14.000 --> 11:16.240
The person you should thank is over there.

94
11:17.320 --> 11:18.240
Ramil.

95
11:24.040 --> 11:24.920
RAMIL

96
11:29.960 --> 11:30.840
Hello?

97
11:33.680 --> 11:36.120
Hathaya's grandmother is in critical condition, sir.

98
11:37.040 --> 11:40.240
This hospital doesn't have enough equipment or staff.

99
11:41.640 --> 11:43.280
Sir, could you please

100
11:44.840 --> 11:46.120
help Hathaya?

101
11:51.200 --> 11:53.400
He asked me to come help you.

102
12:04.360 --> 12:08.880
All right. Now that your grandmother is safe, you can relax.

103
12:10.200 --> 12:13.440
Now tell me, which hotel should I stay at?

104
12:14.480 --> 12:16.400
You're not going back to Bangkok yet, Grandpa?

105
12:17.480 --> 12:18.880
I still have some work to do.

106
12:22.720 --> 12:26.200
If you know somewhere I could stay, tell Ramil.

107
12:28.680 --> 12:30.000
Yes, sir.

108
12:30.800 --> 12:31.760
Grandpa.

109
12:33.560 --> 12:36.160
Thank you again so much.

110
12:36.240 --> 12:39.400
I already told you not to thank me.

111
12:39.480 --> 12:43.400
I'm a businessman. I never help anyone for free.

112
12:44.920 --> 12:46.800
I only do good expecting something back.

113
13:09.080 --> 13:10.160
So,

114
13:11.480 --> 13:14.600
once you think of a hotel for Mr. Pichai…

115
13:18.920 --> 13:20.600
send me the location.

116
13:27.680 --> 13:33.200
I'm going to go take care of Mr. Pichai now.

117
14:05.680 --> 14:06.640
Oh.

118
14:07.200 --> 14:08.400
Has Father come downstairs yet?

119
14:08.480 --> 14:10.920
Mr. Pichai already came down and ate.

120
14:11.520 --> 14:13.840
Then where did Father go?

121
14:13.920 --> 14:15.280
I don't know.

122
14:16.160 --> 14:17.160
Well…

123
14:17.240 --> 14:18.720
Did he go to the development?

124
14:18.800 --> 14:20.120
I don't know.

125
14:20.200 --> 14:22.280
You don't know anything I ask.

126
14:22.360 --> 14:24.120
Why do I even pay you?

127
14:24.200 --> 14:28.120
My job is to take care of the food and keep the house clean.

128
14:28.720 --> 14:32.000
I'm sorry, but I'm not his secretary.

129
14:32.600 --> 14:36.400
You are his close family, and even you don't know where Mr. Pichai went.

130
14:36.480 --> 14:38.840
I'm only a maid. How would I know?

131
14:38.920 --> 14:40.960
Watch your mouth.

132
14:41.600 --> 14:44.440
I've wanted to throw you out of this house for a long time.

133
14:44.520 --> 14:47.720
You're only lucky Father keeps protecting you.

134
14:48.440 --> 14:49.560
But watch yourself.

135
14:49.640 --> 14:52.920
The day Father is no longer here to protect you,

136
14:53.000 --> 14:56.240
I'll be the first one to throw you out of this house.

137
14:56.320 --> 14:58.000
Understood.

138
15:00.880 --> 15:03.000
God, I hate her.

139
15:03.720 --> 15:04.960
Mom,

140
15:05.040 --> 15:08.840
don't waste your time on servants and parasites.

141
15:08.920 --> 15:11.520
Grandpa probably went to the office like he does every day.

142
15:11.600 --> 15:13.480
Then let's hurry to work

143
15:13.560 --> 15:16.400
and make ourselves useful to Grandpa.

144
15:16.480 --> 15:17.880
Okay, Mom.

145
15:17.960 --> 15:21.600
I'll stop at a famous restaurant and pick up lunch for Grandpa too.

146
15:34.000 --> 15:35.000
Grandma.

147
15:41.760 --> 15:43.720
My angel.

148
15:44.720 --> 15:47.040
You're safe now, Grandma.

149
15:47.680 --> 15:50.200
I thought I was dead.

150
15:53.880 --> 15:56.400
What about those two?

151
15:57.160 --> 16:00.000
They've been arrested and sent to jail, right?

152
16:00.600 --> 16:04.320
Mom and her new husband got away.

153
16:04.920 --> 16:06.680
The police are still looking for them.

154
16:08.120 --> 16:10.280
People as evil as them

155
16:10.360 --> 16:13.160
deserve whatever karma comes their way.

156
16:20.440 --> 16:23.680
Wow. This place is as luxurious as a hotel.

157
16:24.320 --> 16:27.480
Where did you get the money for this? Take me home, sweetheart.

158
16:28.280 --> 16:29.600
No, Grandma.

159
16:29.680 --> 16:33.760
You need to stay here and recover first. You still need wound care too.

160
16:34.640 --> 16:37.720
No. Take me home.

161
16:38.320 --> 16:40.440
You'll have to struggle

162
16:40.520 --> 16:44.200
to find money for my treatment again. I don't want that.

163
16:44.800 --> 16:47.680
A kind person is paying for all of it.

164
16:48.280 --> 16:49.320
Who?

165
16:49.840 --> 16:53.400
What a generous soul.

166
16:53.480 --> 16:56.160
Grandpa. My grandpa.

167
16:56.960 --> 16:58.200
What?

168
16:58.280 --> 16:59.880
Your grandpa came here?

169
17:00.480 --> 17:01.400
Yes.

170
17:02.920 --> 17:07.319
Ramil called Grandpa, and he came down right away.

171
17:07.400 --> 17:10.800
If it weren't for him, we never would've been able to transfer you here.

172
17:15.200 --> 17:18.119
One second, Grandma. Let me answer this.

173
17:21.960 --> 17:23.400
Yes?

174
17:25.960 --> 17:29.840
Is Grandpa going to rest at the hotel, or are you taking him sightseeing?

175
17:31.320 --> 17:33.080
Mr. Pichai is at the government hospital.

176
17:33.680 --> 17:34.920
What?

177
17:35.000 --> 17:37.480
Why did Grandpa go back there?

178
17:37.560 --> 17:40.320
Mr. Pichai wants you to come here. Right away.

179
17:40.400 --> 17:42.440
Okay. I'll hurry over.

180
17:47.280 --> 17:50.720
Grandma, Grandpa wants to see me. I have to go.

181
17:50.800 --> 17:54.120
Then hurry. Don't keep him waiting.

182
17:54.200 --> 17:55.040
Go.

183
17:55.120 --> 17:57.400
I'll be back as soon as I can. You stay here and rest.

184
17:57.480 --> 17:58.440
All right.

185
17:58.520 --> 18:00.040
And don't be stubborn.

186
18:00.120 --> 18:02.360
Seriously, you're always stubborn.

187
18:02.440 --> 18:05.360
All right. I'll stay right here. Come back soon.

188
18:05.440 --> 18:07.640
Okay. Lie down and rest.

189
18:08.320 --> 18:09.880
Don't run away.

190
18:19.560 --> 18:21.280
Ramil, where's Grandpa?

191
18:24.800 --> 18:27.560
Go in. Mr. Pichai is waiting for you.

192
18:29.080 --> 18:30.160
Go on.

193
18:35.320 --> 18:36.560
There she is.

194
18:37.200 --> 18:39.320
I understand

195
18:39.400 --> 18:40.920
that government hospitals

196
18:41.000 --> 18:43.800
are constantly dealing with budget shortages,

197
18:44.600 --> 18:47.400
especially small hospitals near the border like this one.

198
18:48.240 --> 18:50.240
So I would like

199
18:50.320 --> 18:52.960
to donate ten million baht.

200
18:58.240 --> 19:02.040
You will present this donation on behalf of your father.

201
19:15.960 --> 19:17.000
Hold on.

202
19:17.960 --> 19:19.160
Let me take a picture.

203
19:21.040 --> 19:23.240
One, two, three.

204
19:23.320 --> 19:26.240
One, two, three.

205
19:29.600 --> 19:31.880
Thank you so much, Grandpa.

206
19:32.920 --> 19:34.080
Why are you thanking me?

207
19:35.280 --> 19:37.240
I was born and raised here.

208
19:37.320 --> 19:40.840
I want to thank you on behalf of everyone here.

209
19:42.200 --> 19:44.160
Burapha was my son.

210
19:44.680 --> 19:46.520
I wanted to make merit

211
19:46.600 --> 19:49.680
and dedicate it to him.

212
19:51.400 --> 19:55.480
None of us choose where we're born. Life isn't a level playing field.

213
19:56.760 --> 20:00.080
I was fortunate. I worked hard and made money.

214
20:00.160 --> 20:04.960
When I get sick, I can afford top hospitals and skilled doctors.

215
20:05.680 --> 20:07.680
But here, there aren't enough doctors or nurses.

216
20:08.880 --> 20:10.440
The facilities aren't adequate.

217
20:11.040 --> 20:13.000
When patients' relatives come to visit,

218
20:13.680 --> 20:17.160
they end up sleeping on the floor or wherever they can find space.

219
20:18.000 --> 20:21.320
We call ourselves a developed country with 5G,

220
20:21.880 --> 20:23.800
but the quality of life for ordinary people

221
20:24.640 --> 20:27.080
is no different from that of an underdeveloped country.

222
20:28.480 --> 20:30.320
Like this hospital.

223
20:30.920 --> 20:33.520
That's why I want to help as much as I can.

224
20:34.240 --> 20:36.200
But it still isn't enough. It isn't sustainable.

225
20:38.400 --> 20:40.080
It's only temporary.

226
20:40.920 --> 20:43.320
The best way to create real,

227
20:43.960 --> 20:47.600
lasting change is to get rid

228
20:48.160 --> 20:50.800
of corrupt government officials.

229
20:52.840 --> 20:56.600
Those people are parasites. They're the real blight on society.

230
20:57.240 --> 20:58.160
It makes me angry.

231
20:59.080 --> 21:01.120
Mr. Pichai, are you ready to go back?

232
21:03.560 --> 21:04.640
You're coming back too.

233
21:07.000 --> 21:08.760
Why do you want me to go back?

234
21:08.840 --> 21:11.120
Well, to work.

235
21:11.840 --> 21:13.920
You'll repay what I spent on your grandma's care.

236
21:35.960 --> 21:39.520
Okay. I'll go back and work for you, Grandpa.

237
21:48.680 --> 21:50.400
You're back, sweetheart?

238
21:52.960 --> 21:53.880
Sir…

239
22:01.040 --> 22:02.520
I came to visit.

240
22:04.400 --> 22:07.960
Thank you so much for helping me.

241
22:08.600 --> 22:11.920
If it weren't for you, I might have died.

242
22:13.400 --> 22:17.640
Please don't say that. Truthfully, I had a responsibility to help.

243
22:17.720 --> 22:21.840
After all, you were my son's mother-in-law.

244
22:22.640 --> 22:25.440
I was a terrible mother-in-law.

245
22:25.520 --> 22:28.240
I never had the chance to take care of my son-in-law.

246
22:28.320 --> 22:29.920
And my daughter behaved so badly

247
22:30.000 --> 22:33.760
that she caused trouble for your family.

248
22:33.840 --> 22:35.920
I'm truly sorry.

249
22:36.760 --> 22:39.240
Let it go. It's all in the past.

250
22:39.880 --> 22:43.560
And you weren't the one at fault. Your daughter was.

251
22:44.600 --> 22:47.680
I can't avoid responsibility.

252
22:47.760 --> 22:50.960
When a child turns out badly, the parents have to share the blame.

253
22:52.040 --> 22:53.680
You're right.

254
22:54.720 --> 22:57.400
Parents can't simply wash their hands of responsibility.

255
23:00.920 --> 23:03.640
I'd like Hathaya to come work for me.

256
23:04.360 --> 23:05.520
Would you be fine with that?

257
23:12.880 --> 23:15.000
May I ask you something?

258
23:18.600 --> 23:20.360
Do you still love your granddaughter?

259
23:23.960 --> 23:28.320
If you don't love her, please don't take her back there just to make her suffer.

260
23:29.280 --> 23:33.920
It's not because I'm selfish and want her here taking care of me.

261
23:34.640 --> 23:37.560
I just don't want her to suffer anymore.

262
23:39.160 --> 23:43.280
All this time, she's done everything for other people.

263
23:44.360 --> 23:47.080
She sacrificed her own happiness

264
23:47.160 --> 23:49.600
for me and for her mother.

265
23:51.400 --> 23:54.960
I want her to have a life of her own for once.

266
23:56.360 --> 23:58.880
I want my granddaughter to be happy.

267
24:05.000 --> 24:06.960
You can put your mind at ease.

268
24:08.480 --> 24:13.200
I'll treat Hathaya well. I'll take care of her. I'll protect her.

269
24:14.200 --> 24:16.080
Hathaya is my granddaughter.

270
24:19.120 --> 24:20.120
Thank you.

271
24:21.320 --> 24:23.640
Please take care of her for me.

272
24:53.680 --> 24:55.560
Where has Father gone?

273
24:55.640 --> 24:58.120
He didn't go to the office, and he won't answer his phone.

274
24:58.720 --> 25:01.640
I sent Grandpa hundreds of messages.

275
25:01.720 --> 25:03.360
He hasn't read any of them.

276
25:04.160 --> 25:06.400
Something isn't right.

277
25:07.160 --> 25:08.960
What if something happened to him?

278
25:09.040 --> 25:11.600
I'm not waiting any longer. I'm going to report him missing.

279
25:12.880 --> 25:16.400
I'm worried too, Mom. Let's go.

280
25:20.000 --> 25:21.160
Father.

281
25:23.400 --> 25:24.880
Father.

282
25:24.960 --> 25:27.080
Where have you been?

283
25:27.160 --> 25:30.680
We missed you so much.

284
25:32.520 --> 25:33.720
Grandpa.

285
25:33.800 --> 25:35.920
I missed you so much, Grandpa.

286
25:36.000 --> 25:38.400
You were so mean for not answering my messages.

287
25:39.320 --> 25:41.520
I had business to handle and wanted some peace and quiet,

288
25:41.600 --> 25:44.880
so I turned my phone off. I just turned it back on.

289
25:46.320 --> 25:48.920
Are you still angry with me?

290
25:49.000 --> 25:51.320
I love you and miss you so much.

291
25:52.680 --> 25:54.040
I missed you too.

292
25:54.120 --> 25:56.160
Where did you go, Father?

293
26:00.200 --> 26:02.520
Hathaya, you--

294
26:03.800 --> 26:04.960
Why did you come back?

295
26:07.040 --> 26:09.280
Grandpa, why did you bring Hathaya here?

296
26:10.520 --> 26:14.400
I went to Hathaya's hometown and spent some time there.

297
26:16.400 --> 26:18.600
All right. Father,

298
26:18.680 --> 26:21.600
next time you want to go somewhere,

299
26:21.680 --> 26:25.880
tell Chayanee and me. I'll take you myself.

300
26:28.000 --> 26:30.600
Thank you for taking care of Grandpa, Hathaya.

301
26:30.680 --> 26:33.960
But now that you've brought him home safely,

302
26:34.040 --> 26:35.520
you can go back.

303
26:36.400 --> 26:37.760
I did not just bring him home.

304
26:39.840 --> 26:42.040
Then why did you come?

305
26:46.080 --> 26:48.560
Did you miss your husband?

306
26:48.640 --> 26:50.120
Is that why you came back?

307
26:50.200 --> 26:51.560
That's right.

308
26:52.160 --> 26:53.240
Hathaya missed me,

309
26:53.880 --> 26:55.320
and I missed her too.

310
26:56.680 --> 26:58.600
I want her to come back and stay here.

311
26:59.320 --> 27:02.360
Then go be sweet with each other at your own house.

312
27:03.520 --> 27:05.360
Take your wife home.

313
27:05.440 --> 27:06.600
Hathaya is staying here.

314
27:08.680 --> 27:12.760
I brought Hathaya back to help with the development. She'll be staying here.

315
27:13.560 --> 27:16.600
Father, I don't understand.

316
27:16.680 --> 27:18.400
Why have you changed so much?

317
27:18.480 --> 27:23.200
I want Hathaya back at work because I need someone honest.

318
27:23.280 --> 27:24.800
Not people who steal from me like you.

319
27:25.720 --> 27:28.480
Father, what are you saying?

320
27:29.560 --> 27:31.960
I checked those accounts myself.

321
27:32.600 --> 27:34.520
Did you really think I didn't know you were embezzling money?

322
27:39.400 --> 27:42.280
I wanted to know whether Hathaya would stand by me or by you.

323
27:43.600 --> 27:45.120
And as for the fire,

324
27:45.880 --> 27:48.480
the reason I didn't report it is because I knew perfectly well

325
27:48.560 --> 27:49.880
that the two of you were involved.

326
27:57.200 --> 28:00.360
What surprised me was that Hathaya tried to protect you

327
28:01.000 --> 28:04.400
even though you kept trying to drive her away.

328
28:04.480 --> 28:05.800
I don't understand it.

329
28:06.440 --> 28:09.680
Hathaya has been good to you, but you respond with pure contempt.

330
28:09.760 --> 28:11.960
Hathaya came here and stole Grandpa's love from me.

331
28:12.960 --> 28:16.280
Before she came, Grandpa loved and doted on me.

332
28:16.360 --> 28:18.520
But after Hathaya moved in,

333
28:18.600 --> 28:21.760
everything she did was suddenly better than anything I did.

334
28:22.560 --> 28:25.280
Grandpa gave her a marketing job,

335
28:25.360 --> 28:28.200
let her sell the houses, and even had her inspect Mom's accounts.

336
28:28.280 --> 28:31.200
You're the one who changed, Grandpa. You don't love me anymore.

337
28:31.280 --> 28:32.960
You don't love me anymore.

338
28:34.840 --> 28:37.800
I deliberately turned a blind eye and didn't report you to the police.

339
28:38.600 --> 28:40.240
And you still think I don't love you?

340
28:47.560 --> 28:49.280
If you really love me,

341
28:51.160 --> 28:53.480
can I ask you for one thing?

342
28:54.120 --> 28:57.720
Please make Hathaya live somewhere else. That's all I'm asking.

343
29:05.640 --> 29:09.000
I feel guilty that your father died because of me.

344
29:10.320 --> 29:11.840
And I'm also sorry

345
29:13.000 --> 29:16.440
I indulged your every wish until you became selfish,

346
29:16.520 --> 29:18.720
demanding, and completely spoiled.

347
29:20.560 --> 29:22.800
If you love me, Grandpa,

348
29:22.880 --> 29:25.200
can I please ask you

349
29:26.320 --> 29:30.360
to make Hathaya live somewhere else? That's all.

350
29:35.280 --> 29:37.640
I understand how you feel, Chaya.

351
29:38.800 --> 29:42.040
I won't live here. I'll just come help Grandpa with work.

352
29:42.880 --> 29:44.200
I'll stay with Ramil.

353
29:46.640 --> 29:47.760
You don't need to worry.

354
29:49.320 --> 29:50.760
I'll take good care of Hathaya.

355
29:52.680 --> 29:54.840
Thank you, Ramil.

356
29:54.920 --> 29:57.760
Then we'll excuse ourselves.

357
30:02.280 --> 30:03.800
Come on, wifey.

358
30:14.760 --> 30:15.960
Grandpa.

359
30:16.480 --> 30:18.760
I'm sorry.

360
30:18.840 --> 30:21.000
Can you give me another chance?

361
30:22.280 --> 30:23.440
Father.

362
30:26.040 --> 30:28.200
I'm so sorry.

363
30:28.280 --> 30:30.520
Please forgive me.

364
30:30.600 --> 30:34.320
I promise I'll never make you upset again.

365
30:37.080 --> 30:39.560
All right. Go on. I want to rest.

366
31:03.000 --> 31:05.280
Don't. Hubby will carry it for you, wifey.

367
31:06.280 --> 31:09.000
Stop talking like that.

368
31:09.080 --> 31:10.800
It makes my skin crawl.

369
31:10.880 --> 31:13.800
And don't ever tell anyone I missed you.

370
31:14.400 --> 31:15.960
I never missed you.

371
31:18.040 --> 31:19.640
Maybe you didn't miss me…

372
31:21.760 --> 31:22.800
but I missed you.

373
31:32.560 --> 31:33.760
I'm kidding.

374
31:36.280 --> 31:40.360
I have no feelings for you. I just can't stand that mother-daughter pair.

375
31:45.720 --> 31:47.480
I'll carry my own things.

376
31:47.560 --> 31:49.800
Go inside. Papang must be missing you terribly.

377
31:51.120 --> 31:53.480
Go. Let go.

378
31:53.560 --> 31:54.880
You really didn't miss me?

379
31:54.960 --> 31:57.400
Go already. And stop talking.

380
32:14.800 --> 32:16.600
Should've let him help.

381
32:23.160 --> 32:25.440
Papang. Daddy's home.

382
32:26.120 --> 32:27.240
Papang.

383
32:27.800 --> 32:29.360
Daddy's back!

384
32:29.440 --> 32:30.800
Come here.

385
32:31.600 --> 32:34.880
What do we do first when we see each other?

386
32:34.960 --> 32:36.200
Hello, Daddy.

387
32:36.280 --> 32:37.760
Not enough.

388
32:39.240 --> 32:41.640
That's my sweet boy.

389
32:44.040 --> 32:46.760
I brought you some snacks too.

390
32:47.600 --> 32:48.800
Here.

391
32:49.480 --> 32:50.320
Thank you.

392
32:50.400 --> 32:52.920
Wait. What do you have to do before eating?

393
32:53.000 --> 32:54.520
-Wash my hands. -Yes.

394
32:54.600 --> 32:55.720
Go ahead.

395
33:02.360 --> 33:04.640
I came to sit with Papang so Max could go to work.

396
33:05.560 --> 33:08.400
Now that you're back, I'll head home.

397
33:08.480 --> 33:11.040
And here. Papang loves this story.

398
33:11.120 --> 33:13.720
He's heard it a hundred times and never gets tired of it.

399
33:13.800 --> 33:15.960
Keep it and read it to him.

400
33:22.200 --> 33:23.560
I want to talk to you about Papang.

401
33:24.160 --> 33:26.320
I'm busy, Mom.

402
33:27.160 --> 33:29.720
Don't waste your time on me. And you don't need to come here again.

403
33:32.360 --> 33:33.760
I can take care of Papang myself.

404
33:35.640 --> 33:38.640
You have to work. I can help take care of my grandson.

405
33:40.600 --> 33:44.400
I already told you. I can take care of Papang myself.

406
33:45.000 --> 33:48.440
He's my son. I can take responsibility for him.

407
33:50.880 --> 33:52.760
Papang is my grandson too.

408
33:54.400 --> 33:55.840
Please let me help take care of him.

409
33:59.560 --> 34:01.040
-Hello. -Hello, dear.

410
34:06.080 --> 34:07.160
Grandma left already?

411
34:09.320 --> 34:10.440
Yes.

412
34:11.040 --> 34:14.000
And from now on, let's not bother Grandma too much, okay?

413
34:14.080 --> 34:16.159
Grandma tells fun stories.

414
34:17.199 --> 34:18.639
More fun than that auntie.

415
34:21.840 --> 34:23.840
I'm going upstairs to put my things away.

416
34:27.440 --> 34:29.120
And don't bother me.

417
34:29.199 --> 34:32.040
I'm going to perform a ritual

418
34:32.120 --> 34:34.800
and cast a spell to defeat naughty children.

419
34:37.560 --> 34:39.280
THE FROG PRINCE

420
34:39.360 --> 34:42.159
Daddy, I'm scared.

421
34:50.159 --> 34:53.159
Don't be scared. She's only teasing you.

422
34:53.239 --> 34:55.199
Come on. Let's eat some snacks.

423
35:03.280 --> 35:04.600
Ma'am.

424
35:04.680 --> 35:07.560
I brought you some snacks. They're a specialty from my hometown.

425
35:07.640 --> 35:09.040
Thank you, dear.

426
35:09.120 --> 35:10.360
Wow.

427
35:10.440 --> 35:14.560
You have to take care of this house and help look after Papang too.

428
35:14.640 --> 35:15.960
You must be exhausted.

429
35:16.720 --> 35:18.680
Not at all. It's actually fun.

430
35:18.760 --> 35:22.120
Sometimes being around children is much more enjoyable than being around adults.

431
35:23.560 --> 35:26.760
Especially a certain son of yours.

432
35:27.560 --> 35:29.000
True.

433
35:29.080 --> 35:30.280
Don't tell him I said that.

434
35:36.920 --> 35:38.720
-Hathaya. -Yes?

435
35:38.800 --> 35:40.800
I need you to talk to Ramil for me.

436
35:40.880 --> 35:42.480
Oh.

437
35:42.560 --> 35:44.480
What is it?

438
35:45.480 --> 35:46.880
It's about Papang.

439
35:50.440 --> 35:51.640
Okay.

440
36:00.240 --> 36:03.160
Then I'll excuse myself. Goodbye.

441
36:03.240 --> 36:04.320
Bye.

442
36:10.000 --> 36:11.360
Hello.

443
36:18.600 --> 36:20.280
What was Ramil's wife doing here?

444
36:20.360 --> 36:23.640
Hathaya just came back from her hometown, so she brought me some snacks.

445
36:23.720 --> 36:26.400
I already told you not to talk to those people.

446
36:26.480 --> 36:29.280
Do you understand? And you too.

447
36:29.360 --> 36:30.720
Don't talk to them.

448
36:30.800 --> 36:33.640
If Chayanee finds out, she'll get angry.

449
36:39.840 --> 36:42.280
-Papang has grown so much. -You don't have to tell me.

450
36:43.000 --> 36:43.920
I don't want to know.

451
36:47.520 --> 36:50.320
But the child you're talking about is your son.

452
36:51.080 --> 36:55.480
If Dad finds out you're talking to me about this, he won't be happy.

453
37:13.040 --> 37:14.120
What are you doing?

454
37:16.280 --> 37:17.320
Where were you?

455
37:18.120 --> 37:20.560
I warmed up some food for you.

456
37:22.000 --> 37:24.560
I stopped by to give your mother some gifts.

457
37:26.560 --> 37:29.720
Don't go over there. They don't want us around.

458
37:31.800 --> 37:36.120
Your mother really loves Papang and worries about him.

459
37:41.840 --> 37:45.040
She told me that while you were away,

460
37:45.120 --> 37:47.200
Papang kept crying for you.

461
37:47.280 --> 37:51.440
And when he was asleep, he called for his mother.

462
37:55.920 --> 37:59.800
He probably misses Nuchwara. He must really want to see her.

463
38:03.840 --> 38:04.840
Go eat.

464
38:04.920 --> 38:07.320
I'm going to bed.

465
38:36.320 --> 38:38.040
NUCHWARA

466
38:39.400 --> 38:40.840
Please leave a message--

467
39:01.000 --> 39:02.280
Daddy?

468
39:06.320 --> 39:07.680
Daddy?

469
39:08.200 --> 39:10.120
Good morning.

470
39:10.200 --> 39:12.200
Witch. Where's Daddy?

471
39:14.520 --> 39:16.120
Where could he be?

472
39:16.200 --> 39:18.120
If you want to know, give me a hug.

473
39:19.040 --> 39:19.960
Now I don't wanna know.

474
39:20.040 --> 39:24.680
Why not? Just one hug. Then I'll tell you where Daddy is.

475
39:24.760 --> 39:26.080
I'll find him myself.

476
39:26.160 --> 39:28.400
Come on. Give me a hug

477
39:28.480 --> 39:31.400
and I'll tell you.

478
39:35.280 --> 39:37.000
Hello, Nuch.

479
39:37.880 --> 39:40.600
Why haven't you answered my calls? How many days has it been?

480
39:41.200 --> 39:45.440
Your son keeps crying for you, you know? You can't just abandon him.

481
39:45.520 --> 39:48.640
Hello? Hello? Nuch?

482
39:49.640 --> 39:52.280
Mommy abandoned me.

483
39:55.440 --> 39:57.840
No. Mommy didn't abandon you.

484
39:57.920 --> 40:00.120
I heard you.

485
40:00.200 --> 40:02.040
Mommy isn't coming to get me.

486
40:02.120 --> 40:03.720
Mommy abandoned me.

487
40:04.720 --> 40:08.320
No. Mommy just has to work. She'll come back.

488
40:09.120 --> 40:11.520
Daddy, please don't leave me.

489
40:11.600 --> 40:14.400
I promise. I'll never leave you.

490
40:14.480 --> 40:15.640
Come here.

491
40:42.360 --> 40:43.200
What is it, Max?

492
40:44.400 --> 40:45.760
What? What happened?

493
40:48.200 --> 40:49.720
Okay. I'll be there right away.

494
40:51.600 --> 40:52.880
What happened?

495
40:52.960 --> 40:56.720
The workers built something incorrectly. I'll have to go and correct them.

496
40:56.800 --> 40:59.280
Go. I'll take care of Papang.

497
41:02.600 --> 41:06.440
But I'm worried that if he wakes up and I'm gone,

498
41:07.040 --> 41:08.600
he'll think I abandoned him.

499
41:09.240 --> 41:10.480
Don't worry.

500
41:10.560 --> 41:14.640
When he wakes up, I'll video call you so he can see that you're working.

501
41:18.800 --> 41:19.640
Look after him.

502
41:45.560 --> 41:46.840
Still asleep.

503
41:48.840 --> 41:50.360
I'll go to the market.

504
41:52.760 --> 41:55.400
I'll buy some things and make you something to eat.

505
42:13.240 --> 42:16.160
-How much? -One hundred baht.

506
42:16.960 --> 42:18.680
Could you hurry, please? I need to get home.

507
42:31.400 --> 42:32.480
Daddy?

508
42:34.560 --> 42:35.800
Daddy, where are you?

509
42:58.480 --> 42:59.760
Daddy.

510
43:01.000 --> 43:02.320
Daddy.

511
43:14.600 --> 43:15.960
Daddy?

512
43:17.560 --> 43:19.360
Daddy, where are you?

513
43:29.240 --> 43:30.520
Daddy?

514
43:37.120 --> 43:40.440
Daddy, where are you?

515
43:41.320 --> 43:43.640
There's no one home.

516
43:46.680 --> 43:49.120
Maybe Daddy went to see Grandma.

517
43:57.920 --> 43:59.320
Grandma?

518
44:05.160 --> 44:06.600
Grandpa.

519
44:07.200 --> 44:08.760
Grandpa.

520
44:10.400 --> 44:11.520
Grandpa.

521
44:12.320 --> 44:13.400
What?

522
44:13.480 --> 44:14.640
Hey.

523
44:15.720 --> 44:17.000
What are you doing here?

524
44:17.080 --> 44:21.160
Grandpa, where's Daddy? I came looking for Daddy.

525
44:25.440 --> 44:28.000
Uncle, have you seen Daddy?

526
44:29.720 --> 44:31.240
Papang, come here.

527
44:32.520 --> 44:35.320
Daddy isn't here. How did you get here?

528
44:37.840 --> 44:40.200
I'll take you home.

529
44:42.520 --> 44:43.600
No.

530
44:45.000 --> 44:48.280
Go upstairs and change. I'm taking you to meet someone important.

531
44:48.360 --> 44:51.480
He has a lot of voter support in the community. Go.

532
44:51.560 --> 44:53.760
Can I take Papang home first?

533
44:53.840 --> 44:57.160
No. I'll take him myself. Go.

534
45:02.960 --> 45:07.200
Grandpa, you're hurting me.

535
45:07.280 --> 45:09.040
You're hurt?

536
45:09.120 --> 45:12.480
Stop calling me Grandpa. I'm not your grandfather.

537
45:12.560 --> 45:14.640
I want to go home.

538
45:14.720 --> 45:18.080
Don't you want to know where your father went?

539
45:18.160 --> 45:19.600
Where did Daddy go?

540
45:19.680 --> 45:21.120
Your father is gone.

541
45:21.200 --> 45:22.480
Where did Daddy go?

542
45:22.560 --> 45:25.760
He ran as far away from you as he could. He doesn't want to see you again.

543
45:25.840 --> 45:27.760
Just like your mother abandoned you.

544
45:27.840 --> 45:31.200
That's not true. Daddy said he would never leave me.

545
45:31.280 --> 45:32.560
Your father

546
45:32.640 --> 45:34.360
doesn't want to take care of you.

547
45:34.440 --> 45:37.960
He wants you back with your mother. He wants you out of his life.

548
45:38.040 --> 45:39.840
That's not true. I don't believe you.

549
45:39.920 --> 45:41.840
Everyone hates you.

550
45:41.920 --> 45:43.480
No one loves you.

551
45:43.560 --> 45:45.480
Everyone here hates you.

552
45:45.560 --> 45:47.880
Go away. Go back home.

553
45:47.960 --> 45:49.240
I hate you, Grandpa.

554
45:49.320 --> 45:51.920
I hate you too. Go.

555
46:01.360 --> 46:03.040
You shouldn't have said those things to him.

556
46:03.120 --> 46:05.680
He might run away, just like he threatened to before.

557
46:06.280 --> 46:08.960
Good. If he does, I don't care where he goes or whether he dies.

558
46:11.000 --> 46:12.360
Where are you going?

559
46:12.440 --> 46:13.680
I'm going to look after Papang.

560
46:13.760 --> 46:16.880
No. That isn't your responsibility.

561
46:16.960 --> 46:18.600
Go back inside.

562
46:19.880 --> 46:21.280
That's an order.

563
46:21.360 --> 46:22.640
Didn't you hear me?

564
46:23.560 --> 46:24.600
Go inside.

565
47:12.360 --> 47:14.200
Daddy…

566
47:15.000 --> 47:18.800
Daddy.

567
47:27.600 --> 47:29.000
Papang--

568
47:32.960 --> 47:34.040
Papang?

569
47:39.440 --> 47:40.640
Papang?

570
47:41.800 --> 47:42.640
Papang.

571
47:51.480 --> 47:52.760
Papang?

572
47:57.600 --> 47:58.640
Papang.

573
48:00.880 --> 48:01.880
Papang.

574
48:02.640 --> 48:05.440
Papang. Papang.

575
48:08.120 --> 48:11.160
Ma'am, did Papang come here?

576
48:12.080 --> 48:15.760
Yes. He came looking for Ramil, but he already left.

577
48:16.880 --> 48:20.560
-Why? -He's not at home.

578
48:20.640 --> 48:23.120
I'm afraid he may have run away like he threatened to before.

579
48:24.960 --> 48:28.400
Then I'll come with you. We'll look for him together.

580
48:29.720 --> 48:30.800
Auntie.

581
48:33.200 --> 48:34.360
Where are you going?

582
48:35.280 --> 48:36.560
I'm going to look for Papang.

583
48:36.640 --> 48:40.240
Dad told you not to. I'm only warning you

584
48:41.000 --> 48:43.240
because I don't want you getting in trouble.

585
48:44.600 --> 48:48.760
I know your father will be angry and that I may get in trouble.

586
48:50.080 --> 48:51.920
But I can't just stand here

587
48:52.000 --> 48:56.400
and do nothing when a child is running away from home with a broken heart.

588
49:00.360 --> 49:02.560
And what about you? You're his father.

589
49:03.280 --> 49:04.640
Don't you feel anything at all?

590
49:18.120 --> 49:19.160
-Help me. Help. -Quiet!

591
49:19.240 --> 49:22.120
NEXT EPISODE

592
49:22.840 --> 49:24.240
That was only a warning shot.

593
49:24.320 --> 49:26.080
This time, I'll shoot for real.

594
49:29.240 --> 49:31.320
I helped bring in customers.

595
49:31.400 --> 49:32.720
They're all people I know.

596
49:32.800 --> 49:34.400
Thank you so much, Uncle.

597
49:34.480 --> 49:37.080
Why are you thanking me? I didn't bring those customers for you.

598
49:37.160 --> 49:38.760
I've told you before

599
49:38.840 --> 49:40.640
not to lecture me.

600
49:40.720 --> 49:43.680
I said go upstairs and pack your clothes. No shame.

601
51:34.680 --> 51:39.960
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
